ed Card Payments. Marqeta, Inc. was incorporated in 2010 and is headquartered in Oakland, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael  Milotich | CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 938 people. Revenue per employee of $666K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $171K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $112K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Marqeta, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.9B market cap on $625M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +6.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 49% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $161M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -11.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 20.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 152% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5163027609252833},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"UBS Group Forecasts Strong Price Appreciation for Marqeta (NASDAQ:MQ) Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/ubs-group-forecasts-strong-price-appreciation-for-marqeta-nasdaqmq-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793925412.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.908,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Marqeta (MQ) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/marqeta-mq-q3-2026-earnings-161653000.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793809630.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.758,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Marqeta (MQ) Stock A